# Local configuration read by `make install`.

# Developer ID identity that signs the locally installed app, so macOS keeps
# its grants only when the new build satisfies the old designated requirement.
# Do not substitute Apple Development for a daily Developer ID release.
# Leave empty to sign ad hoc. Prefer make install-dev for local feature tests.
# Releases are signed by GitHub Actions (docs/releasing.md).
SIGNING_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Your Name (YOURTEAMID)"

# A stable local certificate for the separate AnyDoor Dev app. Required by
# make install-dev; never falls back to ad-hoc signing. Its permissions and
# data are separate from the daily app's, including on the first launch.
DEV_SIGNING_IDENTITY="Apple Development: Your Name (CERTIFICATEID)"
